  "environment_caveats": [
    "live_origin is the Cloudflare Pages staging preview. apex_cutover.completed_at is not set on the client record, and https://dissrestoration.com/ still 301s to a Wix-hosted site (server: Pepyaka), so the apex is not yet serving the Rank AI build.",
    "x-robots-tag: noindex is injected by Cloudflare Pages on *.pages.dev previews. The Lighthouse is-crawlable audit fails as a result and pins the SEO category to 69 on all 6 URLs. SEO is recorded but EXCLUDED from every verdict this run. SEO status is inconclusive - re-audit after apex cutover.",
    "Canonical tags on every audited page point to https://dissrestoration.com/... (the apex). That is the intended production canonical and is not treated as a defect while auditing staging.",
    "DataForSEO on-page returned has_micromarkup=false on all 6 URLs. Verified directly against the served HTML: every page ships JSON-LD (home: Organization, WebSite, LocalBusiness; services hub and contact: Organization, WebSite, LocalBusiness, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList; service landings: Service, LocalBusiness, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList; service area: LocalBusiness, FAQPage, BreadcrumbList). Treated as a vendor false negative, NOT reported as missing schema.",
    "Lighthouse ran DESKTOP only (for_mobile=false) to stay comparable with the rest of the fleet. Mobile scores would typically run 10-20 performance points lower, and the 1.39 MB logo.png would hurt far more on mobile.",
    "Client record status is 'onboarding', not 'active'. build_status is pushed_main and all 6 URLs returned HTTP 200, so the site is auditable and the run proceeded. Flagged rather than skipped.",
    "lighthouse_issues is capped at the 5 highest-impact failing audits per URL per the methodology. is-crawlable is retained beyond that cap as an info-severity entry so the SEO score stays explainable.",
    "DataForSEO's own crawler recorded dom_complete of 3.4-5.1 s on /, /services/water-damage-restoration/ and /services/fire-damage-restoration/, well above the 1.6-1.8 s Lighthouse LCP. Different network conditions; both point at the same oversized logo asset."
